#heading(level: 1, numbering: none)[Welcome]
<welcome>
#strong[R for Plant Disease Epidemiology] (R4PDE) is an online book rooted in the teachings of the annual graduate course, FIP 602 - Plant Disease Epidemiology, a key part of the curriculum in the #link("http://www.dfp.ufv.br/grad/")[Graduate Program in Plant Pathology] at Universidade Federal de Viçosa.

Designed for those passionate about studying and modeling plant disease epidemics with #link("https://www.r-project.org/")[R], the book offers an exploration of diverse methods for describing, visualizing, and analyzing epidemic data collected over time and space. Readers should ideally have a foundational knowledge of R to best utilize the examples.

R4PDE is not a resource for learning data science through R, as there are already well-established books such as #link("https://r4ds.hadley.nz/")[R for Data Science] for that purpose. This book draws on multiple sources, but in some sections, it utilizes data and replicates (with permission) some of the analyses (presented in SAS code) from #link("https://apsjournals.apsnet.org/doi/book/10.1094/9780890545058")[The Study of Plant Disease Epidemics] @madden2007, a highly recommended textbook for anyone wishing to delve deeply into plant disease epidemiology.

#strong[Edition 2] (released 4 October 2026; edition 1 was first published on 23 October 2023). See #link("cite.qmd")[How to cite] for the DOI and how to cite this edition.

The chapters on remote sensing (Ivan A. Lizarazo) and on compartmental models (Nik Cunniffe) were written by guest authors; the rest of the book is by the author.

A mix of general and specific R packages is used to conduct common plant disease epidemiology data analysis, notably #link("https://alvesks.github.io/epifitter/")[{epifitter}] and #link("https://chgigot.github.io/epiphy/")[{epiphy}], both designed by plant pathologists. In conjunction with this book, a new R package #link("https://github.com/emdelponte/r4pde")[{r4pde}] has been developed and can be installed from CRAN using:

#quote(block: true)[
#NormalTok("install.packages(\"r4pde\")");
]

The development version can be installed from GitHub using {pak}:

#quote(block: true)[
#NormalTok("install.packages(\"pak\")");

#NormalTok("pak::pkg_install(\"emdelponte/r4pde\")");
]

This online book is frequently updated and edited. Its content is free to use, licensed under a #link("https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc/4.0/")[Creative Commons license], and the code for all analyses can be found on #link("https://github.com/emdelponte/epidemiology-R")[GitHub]. Contributions are subject to a #link("https://contributor-covenant.org/version/2/0/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.html")[Contributor Code of Conduct], and by contributing, you agree to adhere to its terms.

#link("https://r4pde.net/")[R for Plant Disease Epidemiology~]© 2023--2026 by~#link("http://emersondelponte.netlify.app/")[Emerson Medeiros Del Ponte] is licensed under CC BY-NC 4.0

#heading(level: 1, numbering: none)[How to cite]
<how-to-cite>
The author has opted for self-publishing this book to ensure its accessibility and updatability, reflecting the dynamic nature of the field and the R programming environment. Readers are encouraged to cite this work when referencing or utilizing the methodologies and insights provided in the book. Ensure the accuracy of the details while citing, especially the URL, to direct readers to the correct online source.

This is the second edition of the book. It was first published on 23 October 2023, and edition 2 was released on 4 October 2026. The book is continuously updated: the DOI identifies the archived snapshot of the edition, and the website may be newer. The ISBN of edition 2 is 978-65-02-43127-6.

A suggested citation for the whole book (please use the edition and the year you consulted):

#quote(block: true)[
Del Ponte, E. M. (2026). #emph[R for Plant Disease Epidemiology (R4PDE)] (2nd ed.). Author. ISBN 978-65-02-43127-6. DOI: #link("https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23145652")[10.5281/zenodo.23145652]. #link("https://r4pde.net/")[https:\/\/r4pde.net]
]

Edition 1 (first published in 2023) is archived on Zenodo (DOI: #link("https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23145275")[10.5281/zenodo.23145275]).

