=== Non-parametric (ordinal score)
<non-parametric-ordinal-score>
Because ordinal score data generally do not meet the assumptions of traditional parametric statistical methods, non-parametric methods can be considered as an alternative. Such methods have been proposed for analyzing ordinal data in plant pathology @shah2004. For our example, when more than two treatments are involved, a Kruskal-Wallis test can be utilized. The #NormalTok("kruskal"); function of the {agricolae} package does the job we want. Note that in this case we use the ordinal score directly and not the mid-point value.

#block[
#Skylighting(([#FunctionTok("library");#NormalTok("(agricolae)");],
[#FunctionTok("kruskal");#NormalTok("(dat_ordinal");#SpecialCharTok("$");#NormalTok("score, dat_ordinal");#SpecialCharTok("$");#NormalTok("treatment, ");#AttributeTok("console =");#NormalTok(" ");#ConstantTok("TRUE");#NormalTok(")");],));
#block[
#Skylighting(([],
[#NormalTok("Study: dat_ordinal$score ~ dat_ordinal$treatment");],
[#NormalTok("Kruskal-Wallis test's");],
[#NormalTok("Ties or no Ties");],
[],
[#NormalTok("Critical Value: 52.34422");],
[#NormalTok("Degrees of freedom: 3");],
[#NormalTok("Pvalue Chisq  : 2.529543e-11 ");],
[],
[#NormalTok("dat_ordinal$treatment,  means of the ranks");],
[],
