=== Multiple images
<multiple-images>
Measuring severity in single images is indeed engaging, but we often deal with multiple images, not just one. Using the above procedure to process each image individually would be time-consuming and potentially tedious.

To automate the process, {pliman} offers a batch processing approach. Instead of using the #NormalTok("img"); argument, one can use the #NormalTok("pattern"); argument and define the prefix of the image names. Moreover, we also need to specify the directory where the original files are located.

If the user wants to save the processed masks, they should set the #NormalTok("save_image"); argument to TRUE and also specify the directory where the images will be saved. Here's an example of how to process 10 images of soybean rust symptoms. The output is a #NormalTok("list"); object with the measures of the percent healthy and percent symptomatic area for each leaf in the #NormalTok("severity"); object.

#block[
#Skylighting(([#NormalTok("pliman ");#OtherTok("<-");#NormalTok(" ");#FunctionTok("measure_disease");#NormalTok("(");],
[#NormalTok("  ");#AttributeTok("pattern =");#NormalTok(" ");#StringTok("\"img\"");#NormalTok(",");],
[#NormalTok("  ");#AttributeTok("dir_original =");#NormalTok(" ");#StringTok("\"imgs/originals\"");#NormalTok(" ,");],
[#NormalTok("  ");#AttributeTok("dir_processed =");#NormalTok(" ");#StringTok("\"imgs/processed\"");#NormalTok(",");],
[#NormalTok("  ");#AttributeTok("save_image =");#NormalTok(" ");#ConstantTok("TRUE");#NormalTok(",");],
[#NormalTok("  ");#AttributeTok("img_healthy =");#NormalTok(" h,");],
[#NormalTok("  ");#AttributeTok("img_symptoms =");#NormalTok(" s,");],
[#NormalTok("  ");#AttributeTok("img_background =");#NormalTok(" b,");],
[#NormalTok("  ");#AttributeTok("verbose =");#NormalTok(" ");#ConstantTok("FALSE");#NormalTok(",");],
[#NormalTok("  ");#AttributeTok("plot =");#NormalTok(" ");#ConstantTok("FALSE");],
[#NormalTok(")");],));
#block[
#Skylighting(([#NormalTok("── Processing successfully finished ──────────────── on 2026-10-04 | 20:22:17 ──");],));
