=== Saving the extracted dataset
<saving-the-extracted-dataset>
Now, let's save the #emph[nsamples] object. Just in case R crashes due to lack of memory.

#block[
#Skylighting(([#CommentTok("#uncomment if needed");],
[#CommentTok("#st_write(nsamples, \"./banana_data/nsamples.csv\", overwrite=TRUE)");],));
]
=== Classification of Fusarium wilt using machine learning (ML)
<classification-of-fusarium-wilt-using-machine-learning-ml>
The overall process to classify the crop disease under study will be conducted using the #link("https://www.tidymodels.org/")[#emph[tidymodels] framework] which is an extension of the #emph[tidyverse] suite. It is especially focused towards providing a generalized way to define, run and optimize ML models in R.

==== Exploratory analysis
<exploratory-analysis>
As a first step in modeling, it's always a good idea to visualize the data. Let's start with a #emph[boxplot] to display the distribution of a vegetation index. It visualizes five summary statistics (the median, two hinges and two whiskers), and all "outlying" points individually.

#Skylighting(([#NormalTok("p ");#OtherTok("<-");#NormalTok(" ");#FunctionTok("ggplot");#NormalTok("(nsamples, ");#FunctionTok("aes");#NormalTok("(score, ndre))");#SpecialCharTok("+");],
[#NormalTok("  r4pde");#SpecialCharTok("::");#FunctionTok("theme_r4pde");#NormalTok("()");],
[#NormalTok("p ");#SpecialCharTok("+");#NormalTok(" ");#FunctionTok("geom_boxplot");#NormalTok("()");],));
#box(image("data-remote-sensing_files/figure-typst/unnamed-chunk-38-1.svg"))

Next, we will do a scatterplot to visualize the indices NDRE and CIRE:

#Skylighting(([#FunctionTok("ggplot");#NormalTok("(nsamples) ");#SpecialCharTok("+");],
[#NormalTok("  ");#FunctionTok("aes");#NormalTok("(");#AttributeTok("x =");#NormalTok(" ndre, ");#AttributeTok("y =");#NormalTok(" cire, ");#AttributeTok("color =");#NormalTok(" score) ");#SpecialCharTok("+");],
[#NormalTok("  ");#FunctionTok("geom_point");#NormalTok("(");#AttributeTok("shape =");#NormalTok(" ");#DecValTok("16");#NormalTok(", ");#AttributeTok("size =");#NormalTok(" ");#DecValTok("4");#NormalTok(") ");#SpecialCharTok("+");],
[#NormalTok("  ");#FunctionTok("labs");#NormalTok("(");#AttributeTok("x =");#NormalTok(" ");#StringTok("\"NDRE\"");#NormalTok(", ");#AttributeTok("y =");#NormalTok(" ");#StringTok("\"CIRE\"");#NormalTok(") ");#SpecialCharTok("+");],
[#NormalTok("  r4pde");#SpecialCharTok("::");#FunctionTok("theme_r4pde");#NormalTok("() ");#SpecialCharTok("+");],
[#NormalTok("  ");#FunctionTok("scale_color_manual");#NormalTok("(");#AttributeTok("values =");#NormalTok(" ");#FunctionTok("c");#NormalTok("(");#StringTok("\"#71b075\"");#NormalTok(", ");#StringTok("\"#ba0600\"");#NormalTok("))");],));
#box(image("data-remote-sensing_files/figure-typst/unnamed-chunk-39-1.svg"))

