=== Change severity percentage to severity categories
<change-severity-percentage-to-severity-categories>
Our final step is to convert percentage severity values into ordinal severity levels.

First, let's check the severity histogram

#block[
#Skylighting(([#CommentTok("#uncomment if you need to the read the file");],
[#CommentTok("#ncovar.2021 <- read_csv(\"./data/ncovar_2021.csv\", show_col_types = FALSE)");],));
]
#Skylighting(([#FunctionTok("hist");#NormalTok("(ncovar");#FloatTok(".2021");#SpecialCharTok("$");#NormalTok("severity)");],));
#box(image("data-remote-sensing_files/figure-typst/unnamed-chunk-94-1.svg"))

Next code produces seven levels of CLS severity:

#block[
#table(
  columns: 2,
  align: (auto,auto,),
  table.header([Severity \[%\]], [Category],),
  table.hline(),
  [0 - 1], [0],
  [1 - 10], [1],
  [10 - 20], [2],
  [20 - 30], [3],
  [30 - 40], [4],
