In this first part we have conducted a very important task: to translate UAV multispectral imagery and CLS severity ground data into a single table storing spectral covariates and severity classes which we will use next for building a prediction model.

=== Machine learning model
<machine-learning-model>
Now we will train & test a machine learning model to estimate qualitative levels of CLS disease severity using the previously created dataset.

==== Software setup
<software-setup-2>
Let's start by cleaning up R memory:

#block[
#Skylighting(([#FunctionTok("rm");#NormalTok("(");#AttributeTok("list=");#FunctionTok("ls");#NormalTok("())");],));
]
Then, we need to install several packages (if they are not installed yet):

#block[
#Skylighting(([#NormalTok("list.of.packages ");#OtherTok("<-");#NormalTok(" ");#FunctionTok("c");#NormalTok("(");#StringTok("\"readr\"");#NormalTok(",");#StringTok("\"terra\"");#NormalTok(", ");#StringTok("\"tidyterra\"");#NormalTok(", ");#StringTok("\"stars\"");#NormalTok(", ");#StringTok("\"sf\"");#NormalTok(", ");#StringTok("\"leaflet\"");#NormalTok(", ");#StringTok("\"leafem\"");#NormalTok(", ");#StringTok("\"dplyr\"");#NormalTok(", ");#StringTok("\"ggplot2\"");#NormalTok(", ");#StringTok("\"tidymodels\"");#NormalTok(", ");#StringTok("\"xgboost\"");#NormalTok(", ");#StringTok("\"tune\"");#NormalTok(")");],
[#NormalTok("new.packages ");#OtherTok("<-");#NormalTok(" list.of.packages[");#SpecialCharTok("!");#NormalTok("(list.of.packages ");#SpecialCharTok("%in%");#NormalTok(" ");#FunctionTok("installed.packages");#NormalTok("()[,");#StringTok("\"Package\"");#NormalTok("])]");],
[#ControlFlowTok("if");#NormalTok("(");#FunctionTok("length");#NormalTok("(new.packages)) ");#FunctionTok("install.packages");#NormalTok("(new.packages)");],));
]
Now, let's load all the required packages:

#block[
#Skylighting(([#FunctionTok("library");#NormalTok("(readr)");],
[#FunctionTok("library");#NormalTok("(terra)");],
[#FunctionTok("library");#NormalTok("(tidyterra)");],
[#FunctionTok("library");#NormalTok("(stars)");],
[#FunctionTok("library");#NormalTok("(sf)");],
[#FunctionTok("library");#NormalTok("(leaflet)");],
[#FunctionTok("library");#NormalTok("(leafem)");],
[#FunctionTok("library");#NormalTok("(dplyr)");],
[#FunctionTok("library");#NormalTok("(ggplot2)");],
[#FunctionTok("library");#NormalTok("(tidymodels)");],
[#FunctionTok("library");#NormalTok("(xgboost)");],
[#FunctionTok("library");#NormalTok("(tune)");],));
]
What files are in the data folder under the current path:

#block[
#Skylighting(([#FunctionTok("list.files");#NormalTok("(");#StringTok("\"data/cercospora_data\"");#NormalTok(")");],));
#block[
#Skylighting(([#NormalTok(" [1] \"CLS_DS.csv\"          \"D0_2021.csv\"         \"D1_2021.csv\"        ");],
[#NormalTok(" [4] \"D2_2021.csv\"         \"D3_2021.csv\"         \"D4_2021.csv\"        ");],
[#NormalTok(" [7] \"fcovar_2021.csv\"     \"multispec_2021_2022\" \"multispec_2023\"     ");],
[#NormalTok("[10] \"ncovar_2021.csv\"     \"README.md\"          ");],));
]
]
Let's remind that #emph[fcovar\_2021.csv] is the file containing the dataset we created previously. We will use the #emph[readr] package to read the data as a tibble:

#block[
#Skylighting(([#NormalTok("covar21 ");#OtherTok("<-");#NormalTok(" ");#FunctionTok("read_csv");#NormalTok("(");#StringTok("\"data/cercospora_data/fcovar_2021.csv\"");#NormalTok(", ");],
