==== CLS classification using machine learning (ML)
<cls-classification-using-machine-learning-ml>
The overall process to classify the crop disease under study will be conducted using the #emph[tidymodels] framework which is an extension of the #emph[tidyverse] suite. It is especially focused towards providing a generalized way to define, run and optimize ML models in R. See #link("https://rstudio-connect.hu.nl/caait/")

===== Exploratory analysis
<exploratory-analysis-1>
As a first step in modeling, it's always a good idea to plot the data.

Let's try a boxplot:

#Skylighting(([#NormalTok("plot ");#OtherTok("<-");#NormalTok(" ");#FunctionTok("ggplot");#NormalTok("(covar, ");#FunctionTok("aes");#NormalTok("(");#AttributeTok("x=");#NormalTok("category, ");#AttributeTok("y=");#NormalTok("mndvi, ");#AttributeTok("color =");#NormalTok(" category))");#SpecialCharTok("+");],
[#NormalTok("     ");#FunctionTok("geom_boxplot");#NormalTok("()");#SpecialCharTok("+");],
[#NormalTok("     r4pde");#SpecialCharTok("::");#FunctionTok("theme_r4pde");#NormalTok("()");#SpecialCharTok("+");],
[#NormalTok("     ");#FunctionTok("theme");#NormalTok("(");#AttributeTok("legend.position =");#NormalTok(" ");#StringTok("\"none\"");#NormalTok(" )");],
[],
[#NormalTok("plot");],));
#box(image("data-remote-sensing_files/figure-typst/unnamed-chunk-110-1.svg"))

