The accuracy of the model on the training data should be judged against the accuracy of always predicting the most frequent class (the no-information rate), which is the relevant baseline for this seven-class problem. This basically means that the model was able to learn predictive patterns from the training data. To see if the model is able to generalise what it learned when exposed to new data, we evaluate the model on our hold-out (or so-called test data). We created a test dataset when splitting the data at the start of the modelling.

