In R, we can obtain the AUDPC for the DPC we created earlier using the #NormalTok("AUDPC"); function offered by the #emph[epifitter] package. Because we are using the percent data, we need to set the argument #NormalTok("y_proportion = FALSE");. The function returns the absolute AUDPC. If one is interested in relative AUDPC, the argument #NormalTok("type"); should be set to #NormalTok("\"relative\"");. There is also the alternative to AUDPC, the area under the disease progress stairs (AUDPS) @simko2012.

