To start, we'll need to transform the disease intensity (in proportion scale) data according to each of the models we aim to fit. In this instance, we'll look at the four models discussed in the previous chapter: exponential, monomolecular, logistic, and Gompertz. We can use the #NormalTok("mutate()"); function of #emph[dplyr] package. The transformed y will be referred to as y\* (or y2 in the code) followed by the letter E, M, L or G, for each model (exponential, monomolecular, etc) respectively.

