Overall, the logistic model seems a better fit for all the curves. Let's produce a plot with the prediction error versus time.

#Skylighting(([#NormalTok("epi_all");#SpecialCharTok("$");#NormalTok("Data ");#SpecialCharTok("|>");],
[#NormalTok(" ");#FunctionTok("filter");#NormalTok("(model ");#SpecialCharTok("%in%");#NormalTok(" ");#FunctionTok("c");#NormalTok("(");#StringTok("\"Gompertz\"");#NormalTok(", ");#StringTok("\"Logistic\"");#NormalTok(")) ");#SpecialCharTok("|>");#NormalTok(" ");],
[#NormalTok("  ");#FunctionTok("ggplot");#NormalTok("(");#FunctionTok("aes");#NormalTok("(time, predicted ");#SpecialCharTok("-");#NormalTok("y, ");#AttributeTok("shape =");#NormalTok(" treat)) ");#SpecialCharTok("+");],
[#NormalTok("  ");#FunctionTok("scale_color_grey");#NormalTok("()");#SpecialCharTok("+");],
[#NormalTok("  ");#FunctionTok("theme_r4pde");#NormalTok("()");#SpecialCharTok("+");],
