==== Foci analysis
<foci-analysis>
The Analysis of Foci Structure and Dynamics (AFSD), introduced by #cite(<nelson1996simple>, form: "prose") and further expanded by #cite(<laranjeira1998dinamica>, form: "prose"), was used in several studies on citrus diseases in Brazil. In this analysis, the data come from incidence maps where both the diseased and non-diseased trees are mapped in the 2D plane @jesusjunior2004@laranjeira2004.

Here is an example of an incidence map with four foci (adapted from #cite(<laranjeira1998dinamica>, form: "prose")). The data is organized in the wide format where the first column x is the index for the row and each column is the position of the plant within the row. The 0 and 1 represent the non-diseased and diseased plant, respectively.

