==== Moisture effects
<moisture-effects>
===== Monomolecular function
<monomolecular-function>
For this example, we will use a subset of the data obtained from a study conducted under controlled conditions that aimed to assess the effects of moisture duration on the symptom development of citrus canker in sweet orange @dallapria2006. As in the previous example for temperature effects, the data used here is only for severity on the cultivar Hamlin (plot a in #ref(<fig-moisture>, supplement: [Figure])). The data was also extracted using the R package digitize.

Let's look at the original data and the predictions by the model fitted in the paper.

#figure([
#box(image("imgs/modeling-fig2.gif", width: 5.375in))
], caption: figure.caption(
position: bottom, 
[
Effect of leaf wetness duration (0, 4, 8, 12, 16, 20 or 24 h) on disease severity of citrus canker on sweet orange cvs Hamlin (a), Natal (b), Pera (c) and Valencia (d) at 30°C. Each point represents the mean of three repetitions. Vertical bars represent standard errors. Lines show the monomolecular model fitted to data. Source: #cite(<dallapria2006>, form: "prose")
]), 
kind: "quarto-float-fig", 
supplement: "Figure", 
)
<fig-moisture>


For this pattern in the data, we will fit a three-parameter asymptotic regression model. These models describe a limited growth, where y approaches a horizontal asymptote as x tends to infinity. This equation is also known as Monomolecular Growth, Mitscherlich law or von Bertalanffy law. See #link("https://www.statforbiology.com/nonlinearregression/usefulequations")[this tutorial] for comprehensive information about fitting several non-linear regression models in R.

Again, we enter the data manually. Here $x$ is wetness duration in hours and $y$ is severity.

#block[
#Skylighting(([#NormalTok("wet ");#OtherTok("<-");#NormalTok(" tibble");#SpecialCharTok("::");#FunctionTok("tribble");#NormalTok("(");#SpecialCharTok("~");#NormalTok(" x, ");#SpecialCharTok("~");#NormalTok(" y,");],
[#NormalTok("                       ");#DecValTok("0");#NormalTok(" ,  ");#DecValTok("0");#NormalTok(",");],
[#NormalTok("                       ");#DecValTok("4");#NormalTok(" ,  ");#FloatTok("0.50");#NormalTok(",");],
[#NormalTok("                       ");#DecValTok("8");#NormalTok(" ,  ");#FloatTok("0.81");#NormalTok(",");],
[#NormalTok("                       ");#DecValTok("12");#NormalTok(",  ");#FloatTok("1.50");#NormalTok(",");],
[#NormalTok("                       ");#DecValTok("16");#NormalTok(",  ");#FloatTok("1.26");#NormalTok(",");],
[#NormalTok("                       ");#DecValTok("20");#NormalTok(",  ");#FloatTok("2.10");#NormalTok(",");],
[#NormalTok("                       ");#DecValTok("24");#NormalTok(",  ");#FloatTok("1.45");#NormalTok(")");],));
]
The model can be written as:

$y = c 1 + \( d 1 - c 1 \) * \( 1 - e x p \( - x \/ e 1 \) \)$

where $c$ is the lower limit (at $x = 0$), the parameter $d$ is the upper limit and the parameter $e$ (greater than 0) is determining the steepness of the increase as $x$.

We will solve the model again using the #NormalTok("nlsLM"); function. We should provide initial values for the three parameters.

#block[
#Skylighting(([#NormalTok("fit_wet ");#OtherTok("<-");#NormalTok(" ");#FunctionTok("nlsLM");#NormalTok("(y ");#SpecialCharTok("~");#NormalTok(" c1 ");#SpecialCharTok("+");#NormalTok(" (d1 ");#SpecialCharTok("-");#NormalTok(" c1) ");#SpecialCharTok("*");#NormalTok(" (");#DecValTok("1");#NormalTok(" ");#SpecialCharTok("-");#NormalTok(" ");#FunctionTok("exp");#NormalTok("(");#SpecialCharTok("-");#NormalTok("x ");#SpecialCharTok("/");#NormalTok(" e1)),");],
[#NormalTok("                 ");#AttributeTok("start =");#NormalTok(" ");#FunctionTok("list");#NormalTok("(");#AttributeTok("c1 =");#NormalTok(" ");#FloatTok("0.5");#NormalTok(",");],
[#NormalTok("                              ");#AttributeTok("d1 =");#NormalTok(" ");#DecValTok("3");#NormalTok(",");],
[#NormalTok("                              ");#AttributeTok("e1 =");#NormalTok(" ");#DecValTok("1");#NormalTok("),");],
[#NormalTok("                 ");#AttributeTok("data =");#NormalTok(" wet)");],
[],
[#FunctionTok("summary");#NormalTok("(fit_wet)");],));
#block[
#Skylighting(([],
[#NormalTok("Formula: y ~ c1 + (d1 - c1) * (1 - exp(-x/e1))");],
[],
[#NormalTok("Parameters:");],
[#NormalTok("   Estimate Std. Error t value Pr(>|t|)  ");],
[#NormalTok("c1 -0.04898    0.31182  -0.157   0.8828  ");],
[#NormalTok("d1  2.00746    0.70594   2.844   0.0467 *");],
[#NormalTok("e1 11.63694    9.33183   1.247   0.2804  ");],
[#NormalTok("---");],
[#NormalTok("Signif. codes:  0 '***' 0.001 '**' 0.01 '*' 0.05 '.' 0.1 ' ' 1");],
[],
[#NormalTok("Residual standard error: 0.3296 on 4 degrees of freedom");],
[],
[#NormalTok("Number of iterations to convergence: 7 ");],
[#NormalTok("Achieved convergence tolerance: 1.49e-08");],));
]
#Skylighting(([#NormalTok("modelr");#SpecialCharTok("::");#FunctionTok("rsquare");#NormalTok("(fit_wet, wet)");],));
#block[
#Skylighting(([#NormalTok("[1] 0.8532282");],));
]
]
Store the value of the parameters in the respective object.

#block[
#Skylighting(([#NormalTok("HW ");#OtherTok("<-");#NormalTok(" ");#FunctionTok("seq");#NormalTok("(");#DecValTok("0");#NormalTok(", ");#DecValTok("24");#NormalTok(", ");#FloatTok("0.1");#NormalTok(")");],
[#NormalTok("c1 ");#OtherTok("<-");#NormalTok("  fit_wet");#SpecialCharTok("$");#NormalTok("m");#SpecialCharTok("$");#FunctionTok("getAllPars");#NormalTok("()[");#DecValTok("1");#NormalTok("]");],
[#NormalTok("d1 ");#OtherTok("<-");#NormalTok(" fit_wet");#SpecialCharTok("$");#NormalTok("m");#SpecialCharTok("$");#FunctionTok("getAllPars");#NormalTok("()[");#DecValTok("2");#NormalTok("]");],
[#NormalTok("e1 ");#OtherTok("<-");#NormalTok(" fit_wet");#SpecialCharTok("$");#NormalTok("m");#SpecialCharTok("$");#FunctionTok("getAllPars");#NormalTok("()[");#DecValTok("3");#NormalTok("]");],
[#NormalTok("y ");#OtherTok("<-");#NormalTok("  (c1 ");#SpecialCharTok("+");#NormalTok(" (d1 ");#SpecialCharTok("-");#NormalTok(" c1) ");#SpecialCharTok("*");#NormalTok(" (");#DecValTok("1");#NormalTok(" ");#SpecialCharTok("-");#NormalTok(" ");#FunctionTok("exp");#NormalTok("(");#SpecialCharTok("-");#NormalTok("HW ");#SpecialCharTok("/");#NormalTok(" e1)))");],
[#NormalTok("dat2 ");#OtherTok("<-");#NormalTok(" ");#FunctionTok("data.frame");#NormalTok("(HW, y)");],));
]
